      "id": "S5",
      "status": "pass",
      "analysis": "rowFiberEquiv gives a genuine bijection from A_n to the actual fiber of p_n. This proves finiteness of lifting fibers, not merely finiteness of the quotient. Nonemptiness follows from row surjectivity; beta restricts to fibers using the commuting square and compatibility of the supplied record. The genuine resulting Functor.ofOpSequence is passed to the proved finite nonempty inverse-system theorem with no surjectivity requirement on its arrows. The resulting section is unpacked into the original limit b.",
